@startuml
title Implemented REST index building with CustomThreadPool

actor Client
participant IndexController
participant SearchService
participant DatasetLoader
participant IndexBuilder
participant CustomThreadPool
participant InvertedIndex
participant Bucket

Client -> IndexController: POST /api/index {threads: N}
IndexController -> SearchService: index(IndexRequest)
SearchService -> SearchService: validate 1 <= N <= 64
SearchService -> DatasetLoader: load(resolved dataset path)
DatasetLoader --> SearchService: List<Document>
SearchService -> IndexBuilder: buildParallel(documents, N)
IndexBuilder -> IndexBuilder: copy input; register unique IDs
IndexBuilder -> CustomThreadPool: create N workers
loop worker tasks
    CustomThreadPool -> IndexBuilder: process strided documents
    IndexBuilder -> IndexBuilder: tokenize and check interruption
    IndexBuilder -> InvertedIndex: addRegisteredTerm(term, documentId)
    InvertedIndex -> Bucket: synchronized update
end
IndexBuilder -> CustomThreadPool: await completion
alt all workers completed
    IndexBuilder -> IndexBuilder: publish volatile BuildSnapshot
    IndexBuilder --> SearchService: completed snapshot
    SearchService -> SearchService: publish State(snapshot, documents, uniqueTerms)
    SearchService --> IndexController: StatsResponse
    IndexController --> Client: 200 JSON statistics
else dataset or worker failure / interruption
    IndexBuilder -> CustomThreadPool: shutdownNow(); await termination
    IndexBuilder --> SearchService: IndexBuildException
    SearchService --> Client: error response; previous state retained
end
@enduml
